1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
You by yourself?

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
That’s pretty impressive.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Where do you want to die?

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,000
I’ll let you decide the location.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
I would prefer somewhere remote,
so we won’t be a nuisance.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,000
I wouldn’t want your screams
to bother anyone.

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,000
[growls]

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
[theme song playing]

9
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
CONDITION x AND x CONDITION

10
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
[narrator] Uvogin seeks to unleash
his rage upon Kurapika.

11
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,000
who seeks his own revenge
against the Phantom Troupe

12
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
for his lost brethren.

13
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Both are eager for the battle

14
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
which is about to begin.

15
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
[Uvogin] [chuckles] There we go!

16
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Are these all leech eggs?

17
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Ew, gross!

18
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Sorry for the holdup.

19
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,000
[Uvogin gulping, refreshed exhale]

20
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Got a question for you.

21
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Who the hell are you?

22
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:45,000
You’re not normal.

23
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
I feel extraordinary determination
in your Nen.

24
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
[Kurapika] Before I answer your question,

25
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
there’s something I need you to tell me.

26
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
Do you remember those you’ve killed?

27
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Any of them?

28
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Yeah, some of ‘em.

29
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,000
But mostly just the ones
who made a lasting impression on me.

30
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
This is some kind of vendetta?

31
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Who are you trying to avenge?

32
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,000
The Kurta Clan.

33
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
[pensive grunt] I never heard of ‘em.

34
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,000
The Lukso province.

35
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,000
A small clan with scarlet-colored eyes.

36
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,000
And five years ago, you attacked us.

37
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
[Uvogin] Scarlet Eyes?
What's that?

38
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Name of a jewel or somethin’?

39
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Yeah, sorry, that doesn’t ring a bell.

40
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
But I was definitely a member
five years ago;

41
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,000
I know that much.

42
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
[Kurapika] When you kill people…

43
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,000
people who have done no wrong in any way…

44
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,000
how do you feel?

45
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
What goes through your mind?

46
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Nothing, really. Not a thing.

47
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
[Kurapika] You’re scum.

48
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
For your sins...

49
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
you’ll pay with your life.

50
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Coming across people like you

51
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,000
is the reason killing never gets old!

52
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,000
You wanna know what gives me
the most pleasure, though?

53
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
When someone like you comes for revenge

54
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
and I turn the tables on ‘em!

55
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Those chains are trouble.

56
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
I’ve got no idea what kind of trickery
he used on ‘em

57
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:57,000
but those things are infused
with an unreal amount of Nen.

58
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Which means...

59
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:04,000
That I’ve gotta land the first blow!

60
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
That got him.

61
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Whaddya know?

62
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Even after taking that punch,

63
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
he’s still had the energy to attack?

64
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Least I busted his left arm.

65
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Huh?

66
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Not a scratch? How?

67
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,000
By how much Nen’s in those chains,

68
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,000
I’d say he’s a Manipulator
who controls things,

69
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
or a Conjurer who can materialize aura.

70
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,000
If I had to guess,
I’d say it’s the former.

71
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
But only an Enhancer
should be able to block my attack.

72
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,000
What is he?

73
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,000
-[Kurapika] That punch…
-[Uvogin] Huh?

74
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,000
...was it the best you’ve got?

75
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,000
[ticked-off rasp]

76
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,000
[Uvogin chuckles]

77
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
[Uvogin] Was that supposed to be funny?

78
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:17,000
That was only 20 per cent of my strength.

79
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,000
But don’t worry.

80
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
This time I’ll be sure to use half!

81
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,000
[roars]

82
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,000
[annoyed grunt]

83
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:32,000
[groan of pain]

84
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,000
Why, you--!

85
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,000
[roars]

86
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Dammit.

87
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,000
Little punk keeps darting around.

88
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Know what?

89
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Let me guess.

90
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,000
“You’ll regret that you
didn’t use the chain just now.”

91
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,000
-Right?
-[Uvogin] Huh?

92
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
[Kurapika] Stop making excuses
and fight me.

93
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
You’re wasting my time.

94
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,000
[Uvogin] You want it?

95
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Fine.

96
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:19,000
[yells] Full throttle!

97
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
That’s some intense aura he has.

98
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,000
A smoke screen?

99
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,000
His presence vanished…

100
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,000
He’s using In!

101
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,000
[gasps]

102
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,000
[bones cracking]

103
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:53,000
I shattered your arm this time.

104
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:56,000
When I use my Big Bang Impact
at full power,

105
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:59,000
no exposed flesh in the world can stop it!

106
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,000
But I’m still impressed.

107
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,000
You were quick to react,
I’ll give you that.

108
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:08,000
I’m guessing you noticed
the slight changes in the smoke and dust.

109
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,000
I am impressed as well.

110
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
I didn’t think you knew how to use In.

111
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Striking the ground
to raise a smoke screen

112
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,000
was intended to conceal
not only your physical body

113
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,000
but your entire presence.

114
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,000
However...

115
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
you’re not the only one who can use In.

116
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Huh?

117
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,000
N-- No way!

118
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,000
[Kurapika] See them?

119
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,000
So, you can use Gyo, too.

120
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,000
As you may have guessed,

121
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:50,000
these chains have been conjured
out of Nen.

122
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:53,000
Meaning I can use In
to render them invisible.

123
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,000
So that’s why you kept them
out in the open all the time?

124
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,000
To trick us all into thinking
they were real?

125
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
That’s exactly right.

126
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:06,000
I pretended I was a Manipulator
utilizing Nen-controlled chains,

127
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,000
so my enemies would focus
on what they saw.

128
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,000
And you just proved that it was effective.

129
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:17,000
You see, while you took your time
making empty threats,

130
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:21,000
my chains were already
wrapped around your body.

131
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Capture phase is complete.

132
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,000
[Uvogin growls]

133
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Dammit. But how?

134
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
He has an Enhancer’s defenses,

135
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:41,000
and the Nen in his conjured chains
is incredibly strong.

136
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Has he actually maximized

137
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:47,000
both Enhancement
and Conjuration abilities?

138
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,000
But that’s impossible!

139
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Isn’t it?

140
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:56,000
A Nen user is only capable
of achieving a hundred percent mastery

141
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:59,000
in the type they were born with!
That’s how it works!

142
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
ENHANCER
CONJURER

143
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,000
[Kurapika] Seems you’re
having trouble understanding.

144
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Huh?

145
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Let me explain it as a parting gift.

146
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Huh?

147
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,000
[Uvogin] Those eyes…

148
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,000
Hey, now I remember!

149
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,000
A bunch of ‘em living out
in the middle of nowhere.

150
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
The boss really liked those eyes.

151
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,000
And they were all pretty strong, too!

152
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,000
You’re a survivor?

153
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,000
[pleased chuckling]

154
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,000
I’m fired up now!

155
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,000
How about we see what’s stronger…

156
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,000
your silly grudge or my body, huh?

157
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:47,000
Filthy bastard…

158
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:49,000
Is that seriously all you can think about?

159
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,000
You will never break these chains!

160
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:55,000
[roaring]

161
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,000
[tired panting]

162
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,000
What the--?! What’s wrong?

163
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,000
See, I’m not always a Specialist.

164
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,000
It’s Only when my eyes turn scarlet.

165
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Wait, what?

166
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,000
With my Specialist ability,

167
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,000
I use one hundred per cent
of all types of Nen.

168
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,000
ENHANCER -TRANSMUTER - CONJURER
EMITTER - MANIPULATOR

169
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,000
And the name of my power is:

170
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,000
Emperor Time!

171
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,000
[helpless rasp]

172
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:38,000
[Mizuken] Chains?

173
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,000
[Kurapika] Yes. When you said
I was a Conjurer,

174
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,000
that was the first thing
that came to mind.

175
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,000
[Mizuken] Interesting.

176
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,000
But why chains?

177
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:50,000
It’s because there are some people
at large in the world right now

178
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,000
who need to be chained to hell.

179
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,000
Oh, is that so?

180
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:59,000
Because I can’t shake
the nagging suspicion

181
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:02,000
that you’re the one
who’ll be chained down.

182
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
[Kurapika] What the hell do you know?

183
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Wait a sec! Where are you going?

184
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,000
I’m your teacher! Do as I say!

185
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:11,000
I’m not done talking to you!
Hold on, dammit!

186
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Like I told you,

187
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,000
ordinary chains are pointless!

188
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,000
They’re inferior!

189
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Not only that conjuring
an unbreakable chain...

190
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,000
is impossible!

191
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Really?

192
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,000
Ah, man…

193
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,000
You really are stubborn, aren’t you?

194
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,000
Conjuring unbreakable chains
is impossible.

195
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,000
That being said,

196
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,000
you can conjure something
that’s very close.

197
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Is that so?

198
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:40,000
[Mizuken] Wow… you only hear
what you want, huh?

199
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,000
[Kurapika] Tell me how!

200
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,000
Make a contract with conditions.

201
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,000
A contract... with conditions?

202
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:50,000
[Mizuken] Yes. Decide on a condition,

203
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,000
‘a rule, in other words ‘

204
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,000
and swear to abide by it at any cost.

205
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,000
CONDITION
CONTRACT

206
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,000
A contract.

207
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,000
The stricter the limitation,

208
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:01,000
the more power your ability
will be able to gain from it.

209
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,000
Nen is an additive property,
in most cases.

210
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,000
If Nen adds to your power,

211
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
a Nen Contract
multiplies it exponentially.

212
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,000
(ATTACK + NEN) X CONDITION DIFFICULTY

213
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,000
You’ll need to come up
with a condition for your chains,

214
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:17,000
one that you’re prepared to keep.

215
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,000
But it can be dangerous.

216
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:23,000
This technique can be incredibly volatile.

217
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,000
It’s a double-edged sword.

218
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:28,000
If you break the condition that you set,

219
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,000
you stand to lose your Nen abilities...

220
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,000
entirely.

221
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,000
My only objective

222
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:38,000
is to find my brethren’s scarlet eyes

223
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,000
and capture the Spiders.

224
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:43,000
So, I want chains that they,
the Phantom Troupe,

225
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,000
will never be able to break.

226
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
They will be my only targets.

227
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:52,000
You’ll use these chains
solely for that objective?

228
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Seems rather weak to me.

229
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Let me finish.

230
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Using the chains
exclusively on the Phantom Troupe

231
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,000
is nothing more than a prerequisite.

232
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,000
All right.

233
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Then what is your rule?

234
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,000
I stake my life on it!

235
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,000
Hey… Kurapika…

236
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,000
When your eyes turn scarlet like that,
it makes your aura look a lot bigger!

237
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,000
Hold on a minute!

238
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:23,000
Let’s try the Water Divination again!

239
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,000
[Uvogin] A Specialist?

240
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Most people can only use one type of Nen,
but you use all of them?

241
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,000
[Kurapika] That’s correct.

242
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:45,000
HOLY CHAIN:
HEALING THUMB

243
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:53,000
I can recover
using enhanced self-healing...

244
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,000
easily.

245
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,000
I completely shattered his left arm

246
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
but he healed it instantly!

247
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:06,000
[Kurapika] There were a number of reasons
I chose you as my first target.

248
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:11,000
As you fought the Mafia
and the Shadow Beasts,

249
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:15,000
the other Spiders stayed
completely out of the battle altogether.

250
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:19,000
That told me
that you preferred to fight alone.

251
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:23,000
It also made it clear
that they trusted your abilities.

252
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:27,000
I also prefer to fight one-on-one.

253
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:31,000
That made you the ideal opponent.

254
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,000
You’re an Enhancer

255
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,000
and you’re proud

256
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
of your absolute physical attacks
and defense strength.

257
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,000
In short,

258
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:44,000
you met every condition
I required for my first target.

259
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,000
You’re a test.

260
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,000
If my Chain Jail works against you,

261
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:51,000
then it’s a safe bet that it would work
against the rest of you Spiders.

262
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:57,000
The Chain Jail strips captured Spiders
of their freedom

263
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,000
and, as you may have realized,

264
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,000
enforces Zetsu.

265
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
[gasps and grunts]

266
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:05,000
[Uvogin] I get it…

267
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:08,000
so that’s why I couldn’t produce any aura!

268
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,000
[straining]

269
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:14,000
Zetsu, as I’m sure you’re aware by now,

270
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,000
shuts off aura completely.

271
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Meaning that you would need
to use brute strength alone

272
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,000
to break these chains.

273
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,000
[Uvogin] Dammit!

274
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,000
[Kurapika] If the Troupe member
with the most physical strength

275
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,000
can’t break them,

276
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:31,000
it stands to reason the others
won’t be able to escape them, either.

277
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
His enforced Zetsu is bad…

278
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,000
Really bad!

279
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Nen draws its energy from aura…

280
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:42,000
and if it’s shut off,

281
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,000
you can’t use your power.

282
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:49,000
A technique for sealing Nen abilities…

283
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,000
This guy’s thought of everything!

284
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:00,000
[grunt of pain]

285
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Well, that’s good to know.

286
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,000
It would appear that my enhanced fist,

287
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:11,000
is slightly stronger
than your normal flesh.

288
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,000
That’s valuable information.

289
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,000
[derisive snort]

290
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,000
Provided I’ve chained them,

291
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:20,000
I can defeat every Troupe member
barehanded.

292
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Now tell me everything you know.

293
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,000
Do not leave anything out.

294
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,000
[pensive exhale]

295
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,000
Where can we find the others?

296
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Kill me.

297
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:41,000
[grunts in pain]

298
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:45,000
What abilities do they each have?

299
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,000
[moans in pain] Just kill me.

300
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:56,000
[Uvogin grunting]

301
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:03,000
[rasping]

302
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,000
All of this makes me sick.

303
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,000
The way my hand feels...

304
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,000
the grating sound of each strike…

305
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,000
the smell of blood!

306
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:19,000
Every sensation makes me sick
[seething]

307
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,000
How can you commit such atrocities

308
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,000
and not feel anything?

309
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,000
How is it possible?

310
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Answer me!

311
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:31,000
Kill me.

312
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,000
[grunt of pain]

313
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,000
This is your final chance.

314
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:45,000
I have pierced your heart
with the Stake of Retribution.

315
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
I am now going to set a rule.

316
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Breaking it will activate the chain

317
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,000
and crush your heart.

318
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,000
JUDGMENT CHAIN:
ARBITER LITTLE FINGER

319
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:57,000
And the rule is...

320
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:02,000
that you have to answer
all of my questions truthfully.

321
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,000
Abide by that rule

322
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:06,000
and I will let you live a bit longer.

323
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,000
Tell me where I can find the others!

324
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,000
[chuckling]

325
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Go to hell, you son of a bitch.

326
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,000
[Uvogin groans]

327
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,000
[thud]

328
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,000
[emotional grunt]

329
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:41,000
That probably took me longer
than it should have.

330
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,000
[dialing a number]

331
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:52,000
It's me.

332
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,000
[Melody] Kurapika! What’s going on?

333
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Why didn't you call?

334
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:58,000
-Are you okay?
-Yeah.

335
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,000
[Melody] Oh, good…

336
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,000
How are things there?

337
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:05,000
[Melody] The boss is safe.
She’s asleep in her room.

338
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
Unfortunately, due to the weather,

339
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
her father won’t be arriving
until late tonight.

340
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,000
[Kurapika] Understood.

341
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Thanks.

342
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,000
[Chrollo] A chain user...

343
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Probably a Manipulator or a Conjurer.

344
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:57,000
Uvogin can hold his own in a fight…

345
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:02,000
but one-on-one, he’s most vulnerable
to those two categories.

346
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:07,000
It’s not uncommon for a Conjurer
to enhance the things he creates.

347
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,000
Many do.

348
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:14,000
And some of those abilities
could easily render Uvo helpless.

349
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:18,000
And a Manipulator
could manipulate Uvo himself.

350
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:22,000
I knew it! I just knew
I should have gone with him! Damn it!

351
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:26,000
If he fails to return here by dawn…

352
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:28,000
then we’ll switch plans.

353
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,000
[narrator] Shalnark senses danger

354
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:36,000
as Uvogin fails to return.

355
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:40,000
And their leader, Chrollo
begins formulating a plan

356
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,000
to terminate the chain user.

357
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:47,000
[theme song playing]

358
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:55,000
[Gon] Coming up:

359
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:56,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

360
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

361
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:00,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

362
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:01,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

363
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:03,000
Today, we're introducing Uvogin!

364
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:06,000
He’s really big and a member
of the Phantom Troupe!

365
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:09,000
His ultimate attack
is a Nen-infused straight right punch.

366
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:11,000
[both] So watch out
for the Big Bang Impact!

367
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:19,000
[Gon] Next time: “Very x Sharp x Eye”.

368
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:22,000
It’s so sharp,
it’s like a razor blade or something!

369
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:24,000
[Killua] Whoa! That sounds awesome!
